{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778321-returning-player-unsure-what-to-do-about-10s-in-x20-line","id":778321,"title":"Returning player unsure what to do about 10s in X20 line...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-02T07:55:05-08:00","id":778321,"title":"Returning player unsure what to do about 10s in X20 line...","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> While boning up on the X20 rules for an upcoming game, I've struck become somewhat confused about what to do in the event that one or more 0s come up in a die pool.<br /> <br /> A cursory reading of the relevant chapters in V20, W20, and M20 would seem to suggest that 0 is always a success regardless of the nominative Difficulty and, if the character has an applicable specialty, counts as two successes. <br /> <br /> This seems fairly straightforward, except that a few of the examples (especially in W20) seem to involve players rerolling 10s, which leaves me totally confused.<br /> <br /> Could anyone please help me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1666-firstborn8","name":"Firstborn8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:01:28-08:00","id":778356,"title":"","content":"Difficulties don't get higher than 10, so yes they are always a success. In Vampire 20th if you are specialized in an ability, you can reroll 10s when your specialty applies. By Dark Ages 20th though that is changed to specialties make 10s equal 2 successes which is far superior in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:46:12-08:00","id":778452,"title":"","content":"In the Revised edition (2000), 10s were rerolled. In the X20 rulebooks, 10s instead count as two successes.<br /> <br /> The rerolling examples in W20 were probably inadvertent leftovers using Revised rules. Just go with the doubles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}